This repository is a KIT MEANT TO BE COPIED. Its documented quick-start copies
`project-trajectory/` into another repository, and `bootstrap.py` scaffolds the
templates into that repository's `docs/`. Both are exercises of the Apache-2.0
grant, so:

- The copied kit files (scripts, templates, skills, process docs) stay under
  Apache-2.0. `bootstrap.py` writes the full License text into the scaffold at
  `docs/kit-license`, which satisfies §4(a) for anyone who redistributes the
  adopting repository.
- **The adopting project's own code and documents are NOT derivative works of
  the kit** and take whatever license that project chooses. The artifacts the
  scaffold produces — your filled registries, your requirements, your log — are
  yours.
- If you modify a kit file in your adoption, §4(b) asks you to say so in that
  file. `docs/kit-version` records which kit commit you scaffolded from, which
  is also what makes that delta visible.
